        "created_at": 1794514775.087455
      },
      "rev_n_1_a8b41e_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_a8b41e_1",
        "node_id": "n_1_a8b41e",
        "thought_text": "The previous approach missed updating the result when a better solution was found, potentially leading to incorrect outputs. Instead, we should update the result whenever we find a segment that improves the maximum difference. This ensures that we always have the optimal solution.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_1_a8b41e_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_665947e048",
        "created_at": 1794514796.3405256
      },
      "rev_n_2_1d1e11_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_1d1e11_1",
        "node_id": "n_2_1d1e11",
        "thought_text": "Thought-1: Instead of using a greedy approach, consider using dynamic programming to find the optimal subset of segments. This approach will consider all possible combinations of segments and find the one that maximizes the difference between the maximum and minimum values in the resulting array.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_2_1d1e11_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_1bd11bf8cb",
        "created_at": 1794514825.0702548
      },
      "rev_n_3_632972_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_632972_1",
        "node_id": "n_3_632972",
        "thought_text": "Thought-1: Strategy 3: Network flow optimization\n\nThis problem can be modeled as a network flow problem. We can create a source node, a sink node, and nodes for each segment. Connect the source to each segment node with an edge of capacity 1, and each segment node to the sink with an edge of capacity 1. Additionally, connect each segment node to all the array elements it covers with edges of capacity 1. The maximum flow in this network will give us the maximum number of non-overlapping segments we can apply.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_3_632972_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_7b130491b6",
        "created_at": 1794514851.287027
      },
      "rev_n_4_bc6817_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_4_bc6817_0",
        "node_id": "n_4_bc6817",
        "thought_text": "Focus on segment coverage",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "6861280768019446529",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794514870.5852222
      },
      "rev_n_5_360fee_0": {
